  "what": "Per-tier national and region-restricted variant prices for fast-growing-trees, derived from the retailer's own UCP catalog API. This is the INDEPENDENT oracle for scripts/audit_regional_render.py: it is fetched from a different endpoint than the storefront scrape it judges, so the thing under test does not produce its own baseline (nightly_audits.py RULE ZERO).",
  "scope": "TARGETED re-capture: only the region-twinned plants the D2' audit needs, plus the two repointed handles. It is NOT a full 68-plant sweep -- plants outside this set are absent and the audit reports them as not-checked, never as clean.",
